{
"about": "FIN-896 messaging & internet shorthand pack: the master list behind Lexicons/messaging.json (lexicon-src/tools/build_pack.py messaging projects it), with each entry's reading, evidence and the stack's reading before the pack (before_us). The pack is on by default and every entry is general (heard by everyone); its context-dependent readings are Sources/Phonemizer/Packs/MessagingPass.swift. Tests: Tests/g2p/messaging-readings.json.",
"default_on": true,
"decisions": {
 "owner": [
  "Payam, 2026-10-09: emoji are never read aloud.",
  "Shorthand that can be said as a word is read as the word: 'lol' as the word lol, 'u' as 'you', and by extension 'ur' as 'your'.",
  "Shorthand that can't be said as a word stays letters: tbh, idk, smh, brb, ngl (already letters in the tech list, which keeps them).",
  "On by default.",
  "Hashtags and @mentions: pick sensible readings and document them."
 ],
 "calls": [
  "Initialisms of several words are letters, like idk: omg, btw, rn, ty, np, ikr, ttyl, omw, wyd, wbu, hbu, gtg, g2g, nbd, hbd, tysm, yw, jk, ofc, tfw, ootd, fr, af, xoxo, wtf, stfu, idgaf, lmfao, rsvp. Expanding them ('right now', 'thank you') would put words in the writer's mouth; the owner's rule keeps letters for what can't be said as a word.",
  "Shortenings and rebus spellings of a single word are that word, as 'u' is 'you': abt, bday, msg, smth, sth, obv, rly, b4, gr8, l8r, 2day, 2nite, 2moro. (Core already reads pls, plz, thx, thnx, tmrw, ppl, and bc before a clause.)",
  "Words already: lol, lolz, imma (EYE-muh), cya (see ya). The tech list's rofl (ROF-ul), fomo and yolo are words too and stay there.",
  "lmao stays letters (the tech list's reading): it's said both ways, and letters match lmfao.",
  "Letters a stack already reads right (smh, idk, tbh, brb, ngl, imo, irl, lmk, hmu, fyi, ftw, dm, afk, gg, icymi, idc, tbt, tl;dr, nvm) stay in the tech list rather than being copied here.",
  "Single letters that already sound like the word stay letters: 'r' (are), 'c' (see), 'y' (why), 'k' (kay).",
  "Hashtags: 'hashtag' and the tag's words, split at case changes and digits (#ThrowbackThursday → 'hashtag Throwback Thursday', #100DaysOfCode → 'hashtag 100 Days Of Code'). Saying 'hashtag' keeps what the writer marked; dropping the # (as before) lost it.",
  "@mentions: 'at' and the handle's words (@john_doe, @JohnDoe → 'at John Doe'); an all-lower-case part is read as a name (@payam → 'at Payam', which the names pack then reads).",
  "Emoji: silent, a run becoming one space so the words around it don't join ('great😂lol'). Keycap digits keep the digit ('Step 1️⃣' → 'Step one'): it's a number in a box. ©, ®, ™, ‼ and arrows keep the readings other rules give them.",
  "Text emoticons are emoji too: ':)', ';-P', ':D', '<3', '^_^', 'xD', the shrug, when they stand on their own. 'XD' and 'XP' in capitals stay (Adobe XD, Windows XP)."
 ]
},
"rules": [
 {
  "rule": "emoji",
  "reads": "nothing (a space)",
  "where": "MessagingPass.stripEmoji",
  "guards": "keycap digits keep the digit; ©, ®, ™, ‼, ⁉ and arrows stay unless an emoji selector follows"
 },
 {
  "rule": "emoticons",
  "reads": "nothing (a space)",
  "where": "MessagingPass.stripEmoticons",
  "guards": "only standing on their own (start or space before; end, space or closing mark after); not XD, XP, xP; not inside 'C:\\' or 'http:/'"
 },
 {
  "rule": "hashtags",
  "reads": "hashtag + the tag's words",
  "where": "MessagingPass.readHashtags; TextPrep keeps the # for it",
  "guards": "not after a letter, digit, &, #, /, \\, ', @, ., : or - (C#, URL fragments, HTML entities); not a hex colour (#fff, #1e90ff, #ffffff, #aabbcc); not a C directive at the start of a line (#include, #define, #if...); digits first only before a word of 3+ letters (#2020Vision, not #4B or #12th); #1 stays Core's number"
 },
 {
  "rule": "mentions",
  "reads": "at + the handle's words",
  "where": "MessagingPass.readMentions",
  "guards": "not after a letter, digit, _, ., @, /, \\, + or - (email addresses); '@ 5pm' stays 'at'"
 },
 {
  "rule": "u, ur, urs",
  "reads": "you, your, yours (u'll, u're, u've, u'd → you'll...)",
  "where": "MessagingPass.readYou",
  "guards": "lower case only (U, U.S., Part U, U-turn keep the letter); not after . ' / \\ < > @ # & $ % ^ * = + - ~ | or a letter and '(' (f(u)); not after a number (5 u, 12 u); not before - / > @ ( _ or a point that continues (u-turn, u.s., <u>, u(t)); not next to maths (u = 5, x = u, u + v)"
 }
],
